Explain purpose, conclusion, resulting work and unresolved discussion concisely in the existing summary, rationale and evidence fields. Use sourceConversation evidence for conversation findings and attention evidence for attention coverage. Never automatically rename sessions. Removal affects only the Open Items entry, preserving history and the underlying Run.
Before recommending session removal in Tidy up, establish purpose, useful outcomes and any unresolved discussion. A concluded discussion with verified follow-up recorded elsewhere can be removed with that evidence; distinguish recorded work from completed implementation. Keep ongoing discussion, unresolved choices and inconclusive sessions, explaining why in the summary. Generic titles, empty connections, zero observed attention and idle state never establish completion. If discovery is unavailable or exhausted, keep the session for now.
Keep all discovery read-only. Do not treat status, title similarity or shared parent alone as proof of an outcome. Suggest a new Goal only for a coherent outcome. Never turn a virtual group into a tracked entity.
For followUp, answer the user's question about prior suggestions using freshly read context; for freshPass, produce a new pass. Already-true results are successful no-ops; conflicting items warn independently when the UI applies them. Promotion uses the group's members at apply time.
